WEBVTT

NOTE filter-adjustments: written VO text from episode.json, timed from the timeline VO placements

V0-1
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:06.883
The Over/Under filter finds the
extremes at both ends at once.

V0-2
00:00:06.983 --> 00:00:10.850
It is not a range, and reading
it as one will mislead you.

V1a-1
00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:15.690
All Stations carries the
full count. Beside it,

V1a-2
00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:20.040
the Over/Under tab carries the count of
stations the filter currently catches.

V1b-1
00:00:20.597 --> 00:00:25.034
Until you set a filter, that count
is a dash and the tab does nothing.

V1b-2
00:00:25.134 --> 00:00:28.557
It is not broken; there is
simply nothing to show yet.

V2a-1
00:00:34.593 --> 00:00:39.288
The link below the two tabs, beside
Bulk Adjust, states the thresholds

V2a-2
00:00:39.388 --> 00:00:44.353
currently in force: percent adjustment
over 200 percent, under 10 percent.

V2b-1
00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:49.530
So you can read the filter without opening
it. Clicking it opens Over/Under Options.

V3a-1
00:00:56.503 --> 00:01:04.353
Over accepts 0 to 300 and defaults to 200.
Under accepts 0 to 100 and defaults to 10.

V3b-1
00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:09.070
Each has its own checkbox, so you
can run one end without the other.

V3b-2
00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:12.505
Over alone finds the stations
asking for far too much;

V3b-3
00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:15.570
Under alone, the ones
asking for almost nothing.

V4a-1
00:01:23.217 --> 00:01:27.224
A station is caught if its
suggestion is above the Over value or

V4a-2
00:01:27.324 --> 00:01:31.519
below the Under value. With 200
and 10 set, you get everything over

V4a-3
00:01:31.619 --> 00:01:35.877
200 percent and everything under
10 percent, and nothing in between.

V4b-1
00:01:36.433 --> 00:01:40.117
It is an outlier finder.
Reading it as between 10 and 200

V4b-2
00:01:40.217 --> 00:01:43.643
gives you exactly the stations
it is not showing you.

V5a-1
00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:55.215
Exclude Zeros is greyed out until Under
is enabled, because a zero is below

V5a-2
00:01:55.315 --> 00:01:59.660
any under threshold. Tick it and
genuine zeros drop out of the filter.

V5b-1
00:02:00.210 --> 00:02:04.430
Your thresholds are saved to your own
user preferences, not to the site.

V5b-2
00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:08.750
The Exclude Zeros in Settings,
Minimum Threshold is a different setting.
